    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27643" root="ظلم" body-key="Z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظُلْمٌ</span></b>  [as a simple subst. generally means <i>Wrong,
wrongdoing, injustice, injuriousness,</i> or <i>tyranny</i>]:
see 1, first sentence, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظُلْمُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الارضِ</span> in the CK is a mistranscription for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَلَمَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الأَرْضَ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الظُلْمُ</span> in one place in the CK,
as syn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الظَّلْمَآءُ</span>, is a mistake for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الظُّلْمَةُ</span>.]

